---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../../styles/service.css";

const SITE = "https://www.tmdesignengineering.com";
const url = `${SITE}/services/product-development`;
const faqs = [
  ["How much does a full product development project cost?", "It depends entirely on the product and how far you take it, so I never quote a single number blind. We start with a small, fixed-price discovery, usually a Feasibility Study from £650, and I scope and price each phase from there. You approve every phase before it begins, so cost never runs away from you."],
  ["Do I have to commit to the whole journey up front?", "No, and I'd advise against it. The whole model is scoped, gated phases: you commit one step at a time, each with a clear price and deliverable. You can stop, pause or take the work elsewhere at any gate."],
  ["Where does a project actually start?", "With discovery. I won't sell execution on an undefined idea, it's how projects waste money. A Feasibility Study or a paid discovery phase de-risks the idea and prices what follows, so we build on evidence, not optimism."],
  ["Can you do just part of it?", "Yes. Plenty of clients bring me in for a single stage, a feasibility study, an MVP, verification before tooling, or manufacturing preparation. The full journey is for when you want one person owning the whole path."],
  ["How are you different from a design agency?", "Most design agencies are built around industrial design, how a product looks and feels, and add engineering or \"design for manufacture\" around the edges. I work the other way round: I'm a design engineer who has taken products through tooling and volume manufacture, and I bring in industrial designers from my network when a product needs them. So the engineering that decides whether a product actually works and can be built is the core of what you get, not a bolt-on. I'll also tell you honestly when something is outside what I do, rather than stretching to keep the work."],
  ["Do you do the industrial design too?", "I'm a design engineer, so I lead on making the product work and be manufacturable, and I handle functional and early-stage industrial design. When a product needs heavy aesthetic styling I bring in a trusted ID partner, so you still get one joined-up process."],
  ["What about manufacturing and overseas suppliers?", "That's the end of the journey I prepare you for, and can run. I've taken products into medium-to-high-volume manufacture and can coordinate suppliers and tooling in the UK and China. See Manufacturing Preparation for detail."],
  ["Will you sign an NDA?", "Yes, gladly, from the first conversation, before you share anything sensitive."],
];
const jsonld = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Service",
    "@id": `${url}#service`,
    serviceType: "End-to-end product development",
    name: "Product Development",
    description: "The full managed journey from idea to production, one experienced design engineer owning feasibility, concept and MVP, verification and manufacturing preparation, delivered in scoped, gated phases.",
    provider: { "@id": `${SITE}/#business` },
    areaServed: ["United Kingdom", "Worldwide"],
    hasOfferCatalog: {
      "@type": "OfferCatalog",
      name: "Development phases",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "Service", name: "Feasibility Study", url: `${SITE}/services/feasibility-study` },
        { "@type": "Service", name: "Concept & MVP Development", url: `${SITE}/services/concept-mvp-development` },
        { "@type": "Service", name: "Design Verification", url: `${SITE}/services/design-verification` },
        { "@type": "Service", name: "Manufacturing Preparation", url: `${SITE}/services/manufacturing-preparation` },
      ],
    },
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    itemListElement: [
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: `${SITE}/` },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Product Development", item: url },
    ],
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    mainEntity: faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({ "@type": "Question", name: q, acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: a } })),
  },
];
---
<Base
  title="Product Development, Concept to Production | Thomas McKee"
  description="The full managed product development journey from idea to production, feasibility, concept and MVP, verification and manufacturing preparation, delivered in scoped, gated phases by one experienced design engineer."
  type="website"
  jsonld={jsonld}>
<main>
  <section class="svc-hero">
    <div class="wrap svc-hero-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Service · Product Development</span>
        <h1>Your product, taken from <em>idea to production.</em></h1>
        <p class="lede">The full managed journey, one experienced design engineer owning the path from a first idea to a product that's ready to manufacture, and bringing in a trusted network of specialists whenever the product needs them. Delivered in scoped, gated phases, so you commit in steps and always know the cost and the next milestone before you reach it.</p>
        <div class="svc-hero-cta">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/#contact">Book a free intro call <span class="arw">→</span></a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#journey">See the journey</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="spec" aria-label="Service summary">
        <div class="spec-head"><span>Service Spec</span><span>PD-05</span></div>
        <div class="spec-row"><div class="spec-k">Deliver</div><div class="spec-v">Production-ready product</div></div>
        <div class="spec-row"><div class="spec-k">Shape</div><div class="spec-v">Scoped, gated phases</div></div>
        <div class="spec-row"><div class="spec-k">Starts with</div><div class="spec-v">Discovery</div></div>
        <div class="spec-row"><div class="spec-k">Price</div><div class="spec-v">Scoped per phase</div></div>
        <div class="spec-row"><div class="spec-k">You need</div><div class="spec-v">An idea onwards</div></div>
        <div class="spec-note">Every project opens with a small, fixed-price discovery that de-risks the idea and prices the rest, so you never commit to the whole journey on day one.</div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">Who it's for</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">For founders who want it taken end to end</h2>
      <div class="pain">
        <div class="q"><span class="mk">?</span><p>"I have a product to build and I want one person I trust to own the whole thing."</p></div>
        <div class="q"><span class="mk">?</span><p>"I'm doing this for the first time and I need structure, not just an engineer for hire."</p></div>
        <div class="q"><span class="mk">?</span><p>"I don't want to gamble the whole budget before I know it's going to work."</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="sec-intro">Most of my clients are building a physical product for the first time. What helps most is one experienced engineer carrying it the whole way, with a steady, honest process that keeps momentum without letting the excitement run ahead of the evidence.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" id="journey">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">The journey</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Four phases, one continuous thread</h2>
      <p class="sec-intro">Each phase is a service in its own right, scoped, priced and delivered on its own, and together they form the path from idea to shelf. You can take the whole journey, or step in wherever you are.</p>
      <div class="deliv">
        <div class="di"><div class="dn">01</div><h3><a href="/services/feasibility-study">Feasibility Study</a></h3><p>Prove the idea holds up, the risks, the rough cost, the timeline, before real money is spent. The usual first, de-risking step. From £650.</p></div>
        <div class="di"><div class="dn">02</div><h3><a href="/services/concept-mvp-development">Concept &amp; MVP Development</a></h3><p>Turn the idea into an evaluated, buildable concept and a working MVP you can test, show and raise on.</p></div>
        <div class="di"><div class="dn">03</div><h3><a href="/services/design-verification">Design Verification</a></h3><p>Prove the design works, is safe and is compliant, analysis, simulation and testing, before committing to tooling.</p></div>
        <div class="di"><div class="dn">04</div><h3><a href="/services/manufacturing-preparation">Manufacturing Preparation</a></h3><p>Get the design ready for efficient, medium-to-high-volume manufacture, with supplier liaison in the UK and China.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">One lead, a whole team</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">A team, without having to build one</h2>
      <p class="sec-intro">Most first-time founders don't just need an engineer, they need a team, and assembling one is a full-time job in itself. Working with me, you get one point of contact who brings in the right specialists as the product needs them, firmware and electronics engineers, industrial designers, manufacturing partners, drawn from a network I've built and trust. I lead the technical side and keep everyone pulling in one direction, so you're never left managing a cast of freelancers or translating between them. You get the reach of a whole development team with the simplicity of a single relationship.</p>
      <div class="svc-cred">
        <span class="ci">One <b>point of contact</b>, start to finish</span>
        <span class="ci">Specialists brought in <b>as needed</b>: firmware, electronics, ID</span>
        <span class="ci"><b>Led and coordinated</b>, so you don't have to manage it</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">How I work</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Structure and rhythm, gated all the way</h2>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step"><div class="sn">1</div><div><h3>Never execution on an undefined idea</h3><p>Every project starts with discovery. I won't take money to build something that hasn't been de-risked first, it's the fastest way to waste a budget, and I won't do it to you.</p><div class="meta">Discovery first</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="sn">2</div><div><h3>Scoped, gated phases</h3><p>Each stage is scoped, priced and approved before it starts. You see the cost and the deliverable up front, and you commit one step at a time.</p><div class="meta">Approve each phase</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="sn">3</div><div><h3>The whole picture</h3><p>Mechanical, firmware, thermal and manufacture seen as one system, so decisions early on don't quietly wreck something three phases later.</p><div class="meta">One system</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="sn">4</div><div><h3>Plain-English throughout</h3><p>The decisions, the trade-offs and the occasional impossible spec, explained clearly, you always understand where your product is and why.</p><div class="meta">No jargon walls</div></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">Why me</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">I've carried products the whole way</h2>
      <div class="proof">
        <div class="pl">From the work</div>
        <p>At Ooni I took consumer products from first concept through to volume manufacture, holding mechanical, firmware and thermal roles at once and staying with them to the shelf. That end-to-end experience is exactly what a first-time founder is missing: someone who has seen how an early decision plays out at the factory, and designs for it from the start. It's also why I can lead a multi-disciplinary team well, I've done each of those jobs myself, so I know what good looks like across all of them.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="svc-cred">
        <span class="ci">Behind <b>Red Dot</b> &amp; <b>iF Design Award</b>–winning products</span>
        <span class="ci"><b>Concept to volume manufacture</b>, held end to end</span>
        <span class="ci"><b>Patented</b> technologies shipped to market</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">Questions</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Common questions</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        {faqs.map(([q, a]) => (
          <div class="fitem"><div class="fq">{q}</div><div class="fa">{a}</div></div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band alt" id="start">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="cta">
        <div class="inner">
          <span class="eyebrow">Start here</span>
          <h2 style="margin-top:14px">Ready to take it all the way?</h2>
          <p>Book a free intro call and tell me about your product and where you are with it. We'll agree a sensible first step, almost always a small, fixed-price discovery, and build from there.</p>
          <div class="row">
            <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/#contact">Book a free intro call <span class="arw">→</span></a>
            <span class="price-tag">Starts with discovery from <b>£650</b></span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
</Base>
